// What vision costs the emitter — nothing new, and one bill the emitter had already written.
//
// `packages/wacc/src/emit.wac` is 16,574 lines and nothing here had predicted anything about it. It
// turns out to be the shortest of the compiler counterparts, because **nine of vision's ten
// constructs never reach it**:
//
//     try            a statement rewrite      `./desugar.wac`
//     union          a declaration rewrite    `../../../TECHNICAL.md`, measured and run
//     gen / yield    a machine and a struct   `./genlower.wac`
//     async          a machine                `./asynclower.wac`
//     never          a type argument          `./check.wac` — and see §2
//     defer          a statement rewrite      the `try` pass's shape
//     schedule       a statement rewrite      the same
//     T??            nesting the target has   nothing to do
//     `?.`           an expression rewrite    nothing to do
//     list literal   a construction           nothing to do
//
// A proposal reaches the emitter only if it changes what a *value* is. Vision changes what a
// *program* looks like nine times and what a value is once, and that once is `union`.

import { Decl } from "./decl.wac";
import { Ty } from "./ast.wac";

/**
 * What a union is, after the lowering, in the shape this emitter already uses.
 *
 * `../../../TECHNICAL.md` measured the lowering: `union<A, B>` becomes an enum of one-field variants,
 * which compiles and runs today. `packages/wacc/src/emit.wac` then says what an enum *is*, and the
 * two together price the feature without either of them having been written for the other:
 *
 * > **An enum is one wasm struct**, not a base type with a subtype per variant … a flat struct — a
 * > tag in slot 0, then a slot per payload field of every variant in declaration order … A variant is
 * > then the *same wasm type* as its enum, which is what makes assigning one to the other free and
 * > `match` a comparison rather than a test.
 *
 * So a `union<A, B>` value is `{ i32 tag; ref A; ref B; }` and one of the two references is live.
 */
export void unionIsOneStruct(const Decl d) { … }

// ## 1. The bill the emitter had already written, and vision is what makes it worth reading
//
// The paragraph above continues:
//
// > The cost is space: a `Rect` carries the slots a `Circle` would have used. That is the trade a
// > language with no unions makes anyway, and **nothing here is measuring bytes yet.**
//
// *A language with no unions* is the clause that expires. Counted in this directory: **37 unions,
// 174 members**, mean 4.7 and a maximum of 10 — `std`'s `FileFault`, `http`'s `RequestFault` and
// `mpt`'s `ProofFault` all have ten. Under the flat-struct representation each of those is a wasm
// struct of a tag and **ten reference slots, one of them live**, and it is allocated on every
// failure.
//
// That is not an argument against the lowering. It is that the sentence which excused not measuring
// — *the trade a language with no unions makes anyway* — was true of enums, whose variants are
// written by one author who sees all of them, and stops being true of a construct whose whole
// purpose is to let two packages contribute members to one type. **A union is the first enum whose
// width is not under one person's control.**
//
// The nested form the lowering chose helps here and was chosen for another reason. `http`'s
// `ResponseFault = union<RequestFault, BadStatus>` is *two* slots, one pointing at `RequestFault`'s
// eleven-slot struct, rather than eleven slots inlined — so nesting bounds the width at each level.
// `../../../TECHNICAL.md` argues nesting from `Err(is Corrupt):` needing a group arm, and this is a
// second reason it was the right call, found from the far end of the compiler.
//
// ## 2. `never` is a zero-variant enum and the emitter needs nothing for it
//
// `../../../core/coroutine.wac` now defines `never` as the empty union. Through the lowering that is
// an enum with no variants, and through the representation above that is a wasm struct with a tag and
// **no payload slots** — a type that emits, that no value is ever constructed of, and that costs one
// type-section entry.
//
// Which is the cheapest possible answer and is worth stating because the pages have been treating
// `never` as the exotic member of the set. It is the *only* one of the ten that reaches the emitter
// at all, and what it asks for there is a struct with one field.
//
// ## 3. What could not be written
//
// **Nobody can say what a union costs without a program that allocates them.** The numbers above are
// widths, not bytes: 174 members across 37 unions says how wide the structs are and nothing about how
// many are made. `@/packages/json/src/parse.wac` makes at most one `ParseError` per document;
// `@/packages/rlp`'s overrun fault is raised per malformed field. The emitter's *"nothing here is
// measuring bytes yet"* stands, and vision cannot close it, because
// `../../../README.md` says nothing here compiles — **the one measurement this file would want is the
// one the directory's own rule forbids.**
//
// **A ten-slot struct for a value with one live field is the `packed struct` question again**, from
// the third side. `issues/lang/0074` wants records inline in arrays; `@/packages/zstd` wants three
// narrow fields in a word; and a union wants *one slot reused by every member*, which is what a
// tagged union is in a language that has them and what a flat struct is not. Three shapes, one
// missing feature — a value whose representation is chosen by the compiler rather than by the
// declaration — and this is the first of the three where the alternative representation is not an
// optimisation but the ordinary one everywhere else.
//
// **`match` being a comparison rather than a test is what pays for it.** The flat struct is why
// assigning a variant to its enum is free and why an arm is one `i32.eq`. A tagged union with a
// reused slot would need a cast per arm, which is the cost the emitter's comment is buying its way
// out of — so the space is not waste, it is the price of the speed, and neither number exists.
